            "fame": 32,
            "description": {
                "fr": "La mosquée de Gazi Husrev-bey est située en Bosnie-Herzégovine, sur le territoire de la Ville de Sarajevo. Elle a été construite par Gazi Husrev-beg, un bey de Bosnie ayant entrepris des constructions majeures pour fonder la vieille ville Ottomane en 1531.",
                "en": "The Gazi Husrev-beg Mosque is a Sunni mosque in the city of Sarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina. During the Siege of Sarajevo, Serbian forces purposely targeted many cultural centres of the city, such as museums, libraries, and mosques, and fired on them. As the largest and best known, the Beg's mosque was an obvious target. Having suffered a significant amount of destruction, the reconstruction of the mosque started with foreign - mainly Saudi - aid in 1996, right after the war."
            }
