            "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Istana-nurul-iman.jpg",
            "fame": 27,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Le palais Nurul Iman est la résidence principale du sultan de Brunei et le siège de son gouvernement. Le 9 septembre 2004, Pengiran Anak Sarah et Al-Muhtadee Billah, le prince héritier du Brunei, se marient au palais. La cérémonie, surnommée le « mariage asiatique de l'année », réunit des dignitaires, notamment des membres de familles royales étrangères et des chefs de gouvernement.",
                "en": "The Istana Nurul Iman is the official residence of the Sultan of Brunei, Hassanal Bolkiah, and the seat of the Brunei government. The interior of the palace was designed by Dale Keller Interior designers, and the redesigned Royal Wing by Barbara Allen, Construction was handled by Ayala Abbott and Butters, a UK construction firm and shop fitters, Hagen International from Denmark. The palace had 10,000 people working on it from 17 countries across the globe. It was completed in 1984 at a total cost of around US$1.4 billion."
            }
