                "fr": "Le Caño Cristales est une rivière de Colombie, affluent du río Guayabero, située dans la Serranía de la Macarena en Colombie.",
                "en": "The Caño Cristales is a river located in the Serranía de la Macarena, an isolated mountain range in Meta Department, Colombia. It is a tributary of the Guayabero River, itself a part of the Orinoco basin. Caño Cristales was found in 1969 by a group of cattle farmers. The river is commonly called the \"River of Five Colors\" or the \"Liquid Rainbow,\" and is noted for its striking colors."
