            "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5",
            "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Poas_crater.jpg",
            "fame": 32,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Le Poás est un stratovolcan du Costa Rica. La plus grande éruption du Poás eut lieu le 25 janvier 1910, quand une colonne de vapeur et de cendres s'éleva à 8 000 mètres au-dessus du cratère. Cette éruption produisit 640 000 tonnes de cendres. Entre 1952 et 1954, le Poás a bombardé les proches environs de cendres et de scories. En 1989, le parc national a été obligé de fermer à cause de dangereuses émissions de gaz soufrés.",
                "en": "The Poás Volcano, is an active 2,697-metre stratovolcano in central Costa Rica located within Poas Volcano National Park. As of September 1, 2018, the National Park has re-opened with limited access and revised regulations. Visitors are required to make an online reservation to enter the park and the number of visitors and time allowed at the crater is limited. Only the main crater observation area is open as of September 2018. As of April 2023, while some adjacent trails remain closed, the trail to the Lake Botos is open."
            }
