            "fame": 42,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Le lac Abbe, Abbé, Abhé ou Abhe Bad est un lac salé endoréique d'Afrique de l'Est situé sur la frontière entre Djibouti et l'Éthiopie, à l'extrémité de la vallée de l'Awash et l'extrémité occidentale du grand bassin du Gobaad.",
                "en": "Lake Abbe, also known as Lake Abhe Bad, is a salt lake, lying on the Ethiopia-Djibouti border. It is one of a chain of six connected lakes, which also includes lakes Gargori, Laitali, Gummare, Bario and Afambo. The lake is the ultimate destination of the Awash River, which is at the center of the Afar Triangle. Lake Abbe is considered one of the most inaccessible areas of the earth. The water itself is known for its flamingos."
            }
