            "license": "CC BY 3.0",
            "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0",
            "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rauma_3.jpg",
            "fame": 37,
            "description": {
                "fr": "La vieille ville de Rauma ou ancienne Rauma selon la dénomination de l'UNESCO est le centre historique de la ville de Rauma en Finlande, inscrite depuis 1991 sur la liste du patrimoine mondial de l'UNESCO.",
                "en": "Old Rauma is the wooden centre of the town of Rauma, Finland. It was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List in 1991 because of its unique wooden architecture and its well-preserved medieval town layout. It is one of the only medieval towns in Finland. The area of Old Rauma is about 0.3 km2, with approximately six hundred buildings and about 800 people living in the area. The oldest buildings date from the 18th century, as two fires in 1640 and 1682 destroyed much of the town."
            }
