            "author": "NASA",
            "license": "Public domain",
            "licenseUrl": null,
            "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lago_de_Atitlan_seen_from_orbit.jpg",
            "fame": 41,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Le lac Atitlán est un lac endoréique du sud-ouest du Guatemala, situé à 108 km à l'ouest de la capitale Guatemala. Trois caldeiras géantes se seraient succédé au cours de trois phases volcaniques distinctes, la plus ancienne débutant il y a 14 millions d'années.",
                "en": "Lake Atitlán is a large natural lake in the Guatemalan Highlands of the Sierra Madre mountain range. San Pedro is the oldest of the three and appears to have ceased erupting approximately 40,000 years ago. Tolimán began growing after San Pedro ceased erupting and likely remains active, although it has not erupted historically. Atitlán has formed almost entirely in the last 10,000 years and remains active; its most recent eruption occurred in 1853. On February 4, 1976, a massive earthquake struck Guatemala, killing more than 26,000 people."
            }
