                "fr": "L'Anneau du Kerry est un circuit touristique du comté de Kerry, au sud-ouest de l'Irlande, qui fait le tour de la péninsule d'Iveragh.",
                "en": "The Ring of Kerry is a 179-kilometre-long circular tourist route in County Kerry, south-western Ireland. Clockwise from Killarney it follows the N71 to Kenmare, then the N70 around the Iveragh Peninsula to Killorglin – passing through Sneem, Waterville, Cahersiveen, and Glenbeigh – before returning to Killarney via the N72."
