            "fame": 76,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Le fort Rouge, aussi appelé palais-fort de Shahjahanabad ou Lal Qil'ah est une forteresse et une ancienne résidence impériale d'architecture moghole à Delhi en Inde. Le fort Rouge a été construit par l'empereur moghol Shâh Jahân entre 1638 et 1648.",
                "en": "The Red Fort is a historic Mughal fort located in the Old Delhi area of Delhi, India. In 1712, Jahandar Shah was crowned the Mughal Emperor. Within a year of beginning his rule, Shah was murdered and replaced by Farrukhsiyar. In 1739, the Persian emperor Nadir Shah decisively defeated the Mughal army, despite its considerable strength of approximately 200,000 soldiers. Following his victory, he plundered the Red Fort, seizing its treasures, including the legendary Peacock Throne."
            }
