            "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0",
            "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pamban_bridge_near_rameshwaram.JPG",
            "fame": 24,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Le pont de Pamban était un pont ferroviaire reliant la ville de Rameswaram, sur l’île de Pamban, à Mandapam, sur le territoire continental de l’Inde. Le pont fut ouvert à la circulation le 24 février 1914 et reliait Rameswaram, sur l’île de Pamban, au continent indien. Il fut endommagé lors du cyclone de Rameswaram de 1964 et nécessita d’importants travaux de réparation. Le pont routier adjacent fut ouvert en 1988. En 2009, de nouveaux travaux de renforcement furent réalisés sur le pont sous la supervision de E.",
                "en": "Pamban Bridge was a railway bridge that connected the town of Rameswaram on Pamban Island with Mandapam in mainland India. The bridge was opened for traffic on 24 February 1914 and connected Rameshwaram in Pamban Island with mainland India. The bridge was damaged during the 1964 Rameswaram cyclone and required extensive repair work. The adjacent road bridge was opened in 1988. In 2009, further strengthening work was carried out on the bridge under the supervision of E."
            }
