            "fame": 125,
            "description": {
                "fr": "L'Etna est un volcan d'Italie situé en Sicile, à proximité de la ville de Catane, la deuxième ville la plus peuplée de Sicile. Gente dell'Etna, court métrage documentaire de Corrado Sofia, Italie, 1958, 10 min. Porcherie, film de fiction italo-français de Pier Paolo Pasolini, 1969, 98 min. Fermata Etna, téléfilm de Klaus-Michael Grüber, Italie, 1981. Le Choix des seigneurs, film de Giacomo Battiato, Italie, 1983, 100 min.",
                "en": "Mount Etna, or simply Etna, is an active stratovolcano on the east coast of Sicily, Italy, in the Metropolitan City of Catania, between the cities of Messina and Catania. Caesarius employs in his account the Latin phrase in monte Gyber to describe the location of Arthur's kingdom. The Fada de Gibel of the Castle of Gibaldar appears in Jaufre, the only surviving Arthurian romance in the Occitan language, the composition of which is dated to between 1180 and 1230."
            }
