                "fr": "La mer Morte est un lac salé du Proche-Orient partagé entre Israël, la Jordanie et la Cisjordanie. En 1837, Gotthilf Heinrich von Schubert est le premier, avec son compagnon de voyage Johannes Roth, à relever que le niveau de la mer Morte est de plusieurs centaines de mètres au-dessous de celui de la Méditerranée.",
                "en": "The Dead Sea, also known by other names, is a landlocked salt lake bordered by Jordan to the east, the West Bank to the west and Israel to the southwest. However, he referred to the lake by its Greek name, Asphaltites. Herod the Great, king of Judaea, built or rebuilt several fortresses and palaces along the western shore of the Dead Sea, with Masada being the most famous."
