                "fr": "Le Kinkaku-ji",
                "en": "Kinkaku-ji, officially named Rokuon-ji, is a Zen Buddhist temple in Kyoto, Japan and a tourist attraction. During the fire, the original statue of Ashikaga Yoshimitsu was lost to the flames. A fictionalized version of these events is at the center of Yukio Mishima's 1956 book The Temple of the Golden Pavilion, and another in the ballet RAkU. The present pavilion structure dates from 1955, when it was rebuilt."
