                "fr": "La cathédrale de Vilnius ou basilique archicathédrale Saint-Stanislas-et-Saint-Ladislas de Vilnius",
                "en": "The Vilnius Cathedral, formally the Archcathedral Basilica of St. The first securely documented cathedral was founded on the initiative of Jogaila following the Christianization of Lithuania in 1387 and was consecrated in 1388. After the cathedral was destroyed by fire in 1419, Vytautas had a substantially larger Gothic hall church built in its place."
