            "fame": 15,
            "description": {
                "fr": "L'ancienne ville de Ghadamès est la partie ancienne de la ville de Ghadamès, en Libye et l'une des principales villes du désert de Libye. Bâtie dans une oasis, Ghadamès, « la perle du désert», est une des plus anciennes cités présahariennes et un exemple exceptionnel d'habitat traditionnel.",
                "en": "The Old town of Ghadames is the old city of the modern city of Ghadames, Libya and one of Libya's major desert cities. Houses in Ghadames are typically four stories tall, built using local materials like mud brick, limestone, and palm wood for reinforcement and roofing. The vertical layout of the homes was organized by function: The ground floor was used for storage of supplies. The first floor was the main family living quarters, often centered around a main room or hall known as the wast ad-dar."
            }
