            "fame": 42,
            "description": {
                "fr": "La mosquée Koutoubia est un édifice religieux construit au XIIe siècle à Marrakech, Maroc. Marrakech fut fondée en 1070 par le sultan Almoravide Youssef Ben Tachfine et Zaynab Nefzaouia. En 1147, le sultan Almohade Abdelmoumen conquiert la ville.",
                "en": "The Kutubiyya Mosque or Koutoubia Mosque is the largest mosque in Marrakesh, Morocco. It is believed that the minbar was originally placed in the first Ben Youssef Mosque. It was then transferred by the Almohad ruler Abd al-Mu'min to the first Kutubiyya Mosque and was later moved to the second incarnation of that mosque. It remained there until 1962, when it was moved to the El Badi Palace where it is now on display for visitors."
            }
