            "licenseUrl": null,
            "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Volcan_baru.jpg",
            "fame": 38,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Le Barú ou Volcán de Chiriquí est un volcan endormi de la cordillère de Talamanca, à l'Ouest du Panama. Des recherches archéologiques ont montré la présence de peuplements aux abords du volcan Barú entre les années 300 av.",
                "en": "The Volcán Barú is an active stratovolcano and the tallest mountain in Panama, at 3,475 metres high. They also showed that the youngest volcanism consists primarily of adakites whereas the older volcanism is normal calc-alkaline lavas. USGS Volcano-Hazards Assessment Study In 2006, an earthquake swarm was registered in the Volcán Barú area. This was not the first one; researchers cite at least three other seismic events of the same nature recorded in the recent past."
            }
