                "fr": "Mohenjo-daro, est un site majeur de la civilisation de la vallée de l'Indus. La ville a été successivement détruite et reconstruite au moins sept fois.",
                "en": "Mohenjo-daro is an archaeological site in the Larkana District of Sindh, Pakistan. An initial agreement to fund restoration was agreed through UNESCO in Paris on 27 May 1980. Contributions were made by a number of other countries to the project: Preservation work for Mohenjo-daro was suspended in December 1996 after funding from the Pakistani government and international organizations stopped. Site conservation work resumed in April 1997, using funds made available by the UNESCO."
