            "fame": 36,
            "description": {
                "fr": "La vallée de la Hunza est une vallée située dans la région autonome du Gilgit-Baltistan, au Pakistan. Le Hunza était un État princier bordant l'Ouïghourstan au nord-est et le Pamir au nord-ouest, jusqu'à sa dissolution en 1974, par Zulfikar Ali Bhutto.",
                "en": "The Hunza Valley, also known as the Hunza-Nagar Valley, is a mountainous river valley traversed by the Hunza River in Gilgit-Baltistan region, in Pakistan-administered Kashmir. The scouts opened fire on the demonstrators in Chalt, killing nine people and wounding many more. The leaders of the protest were imprisoned. Later, on 25 September 1974, Prime Minister of Pakistan Zulfiqar Ali Bhutto dissolved the princely states of Nagar and Hunza, set the prisoners free and gave democratic representation to the Northern Areas Council, now the Gilgit-Baltistan Assembly."
            }
