            "fame": 20,
            "description": {
                "fr": "La Librairie Lello ou Librairie Lello et Irmão ou Librairie Chardron est une librairie-maison d'édition néogothique-Art nouveau du XIXe siècle, du centre historique de Porto au Portugal. Suite à la disparation de son fondateur à l'âge de 45 ans, la librairie est vendue au groupe Lugan & Genelioux Sucessores. En 1894, Mathieux Lugan a revendu l'ancienne librairie Chardron aux frères José et António Lello.",
                "en": "The Livraria Lello & Irmão, commonly known in English as the Lello Bookshop, is a bookshop located in the civil parish of Cedofeita, Santo Ildefonso, Sé, Miragaia, São Nicolau e Vitória, in the northern Portuguese municipality of Porto. These purchases later included the 7 April 1898 sale of the firm Livraria Lemos & Co. The brothers hired engineer Francisco Xavier Esteves to construct the new bookstore on Rua das Carmelitas. In 1906, the Livraria Lello was inaugurated. By 1919, the bookstore was simply designated as the Lello & Irmão, Lda."
            }
