                "en": "The Jules Wijdenbosch Bridge, also called Suriname bridge and known locally as Bosje Brug, is a concrete road bridge over the Suriname River between the capital city Paramaribo and Meerzorg in the Commewijne District. The bridge is part of the East-West Link, and is named after former president Jules Wijdenbosch, who opened it. Constructed by Dutch constructor Ballast-Nedam, the bridge has two lanes, is 1504 metres long, and was opened on 20 May 2000."
