                "fr": "Le Wat Arun",
                "en": "Wat Arun Ratchawararam Ratchawaramahawihan or Wat Arun is a Buddhist temple in the Bangkok Yai district of Bangkok, Thailand. The main prang was completed in 1851, after nine years of continued construction. In 1858, Henri Mouhot, a French explorer, recorded the detailed observations of Wat Chang in his travel journals Voyage dans les royaumes de Siam, de Cambodge, de Laos when he had journeyed to Siam."
