                "fr": "Le parc national Nino Konis Santana est le premier parc national du Timor oriental, créé le 3 août 2007. La partie terrestre relie trois zones ornithologiques de première importance: Lore, Monte Paitchau et le lac Iralalara, et l'île Jaco.",
                "en": "Nino Konis Santana National Park is Timor-Leste's first national park. In June 2026, UNESCO designated Nino Konis Santana National Park as Timor-Leste's first Biosphere Reserve under its Man and the Biosphere Programme. The designation recognised the park for its exceptional combination of terrestrial and marine ecosystems, including the country's largest remaining primary forests, extensive coral reefs within the Coral Triangle, and the rich cultural heritage of the Fataluku people."
