            "fame": 60,
            "description": {
                "fr": "Le palais du Vatican ou, selon sa dénomination officielle, le Palais apostolique est une des résidences des papes au Vatican depuis leur retour d'exil d'Avignon. Au Ve siècle, le pape Symmaque fait construire un palais pontifical proche de la première basilique Saint-Pierre et qui constitue une résidence alternative au palais du Latran.",
                "en": "The Apostolic Palace is the official residence of the Pope, the head of the Catholic Church, located in Vatican City. The major additions and decorations of the palace are the work of the following popes for 150 years. Construction of the current version of the palace began on 30 April 1589 under Pope Sixtus V and its various intrinsic parts were completed by later successors, Pope Urban VII, Pope Innocent XI and Pope Clement VIII. In the 20th century, Pope Pius XI built a monumental art gallery and museum entrance. Construction of the Palace took place mainly between 1471 and 1605."
            }
