                "en": "Norfolk Island National Park is a protected area of 6.50 km2 located at 29°2′0″S 167°56′59″E in the South Pacific Ocean, about 1,471 kilometres off the East coast of Australia. The park’s area includes the Mount Pitt section on the namesake Norfolk Island with an area of 4.60 km2 / 460 ha, as well as the neighbouring Phillip Island encompassing 1.90 km2 / 190 ha, and the much smaller Nepean Island."
